.TH AI-REVIVE-RESUMERS 7 "September 2026" "ai-revive 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
ai-revive-resumers \- how ai-revive relaunches the program that ran in a pane
.SH DESCRIPTION
When
.BR ai-revive (1)
saves a snapshot it runs every
.I resumer
against every pane. A resumer is an executable that looks at the pane (its shell's pid, working
directory and foreground command) and either claims it, printing the command that brings the
program back, or passes. Resumers are tried in name order; the first claim wins.
.SH LOCATIONS
.TP
.I /usr/share/ai-revive/resumers/
Shipped resumers.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ai-revive/resumers/
User resumers. A file with the same name as a shipped one replaces it; a new name adds one.
Names start with two digits that fix the order, e.g.
.IR 15\-codex .
.SH SHIPPED RESUMERS
.TP
.B 10-claude
Claude Code registers every interactive process in
.I ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json
together with the tmux pane it runs in. The resumer finds the record for the pane, checks that
the pid still belongs to that process, and emits
.B claude \-\-resume
.I session-id
with the conversation's directory. Two Claude panes in the same directory therefore come back as
two different conversations. A Claude without a record (started seconds ago) falls back to
.BR "claude \-\-continue" .
.TP
.B 20-ssh
Claims a pane whose foreground command is
.B ssh
and whose shell has an
.B ssh
child; emits that child's exact command line. Transports started by git, scp or rsync are not
direct children of the shell and are left alone.
.TP
.B 90-whitelist
Claims a pane whose shell has a child named in the
.B RESUME_COMMANDS
setting and emits its command line.
.SH CONTRACT
A resumer is invoked as
.B <resumer> probe
with these variables in the environment:
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_PANE_ID
The tmux pane id, e.g.
.IR %38 .
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_PANE_PID
Pid of the pane's shell; the program is normally a direct child.
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_WINDOW_ID
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_SESSION
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_CWD
The pane's current directory.
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_COMMAND
The pane's foreground command as tmux reports it
.RI ( #{pane_current_command} ).
.TP
.BI AI_REVIVE_ KEY
Every configuration key, e.g.
.BR AI_REVIVE_RESUME_COMMANDS .
.TP
.B AI_REVIVE_HOME
The installation directory;
.I $AI_REVIVE_HOME/lib/common.sh
can be sourced for helpers such as
.BR shell_quote ,
.B proc_cmdline_to_shell
and
.BR children_of .
.PP
To claim the pane the resumer exits 0 and prints one JSON object:
.PP
.nf
  {"cmd": "claude --resume 12345678-...", "cwd": "/home/me/proj", "meta": {...}}
.fi
.PP
.B cmd
is typed into the restored pane's shell after
.BI "cd " cwd
(default: the pane's directory) and must therefore be shell-safe; use
.B shell_quote
or
.BR proc_cmdline_to_shell .
.B meta
is stored in the snapshot for display and debugging. Exit 1 passes the pane on to the next
resumer. Any other exit status, output that is not JSON, or more than 5 seconds of runtime is
logged and treated as a pass.
.PP
.B <resumer> info
prints a one-line description for
.BR "ai-revive resumers" .
.SH EXAMPLE
A resumer for a program that is restarted with the same arguments:
.PP
.nf
  #!/usr/bin/env bash
  set -euo pipefail
  . "$AI_REVIVE_HOME/lib/common.sh"
  case ${1:-} in
    info) echo "myprog: restart with the same arguments"; exit 0 ;;
    probe) ;;
    *) exit 2 ;;
  esac
  for child in $(children_of "$AI_REVIVE_PANE_PID"); do
    [ "$(proc_argv0 "$child")" = myprog ] || continue
    jq -cn --arg cmd "$(proc_cmdline_to_shell "$child")" '{cmd: $cmd, meta: {}}'
    exit 0
  done
  exit 1
.fi
.PP
Try it on a live pane with
.B ai-revive resumers probe
.IR %id .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ai-revive (1)
